# Tiptap Editor — Rich Text Editor Rules

## Installation

Core packages:
- `@tiptap/react` — React bindings and core functionality
- `@tiptap/pm` — ProseMirror dependencies (required)
- `@tiptap/starter-kit` — Common extensions bundle (paragraphs, headings, bold, italic, lists, history)
- `@tiptap/extensions` — All official extensions (install individually for smaller bundles)

## Editor Setup

### Hook-Based Approach (Simple UIs)

```tsx
import { useEditor, EditorContent } from "@tiptap/react";
import StarterKit from "@tiptap/starter-kit";
import Placeholder from "@tiptap/extension-placeholder";

interface ResumeEditorProps {
  content?: string;
  onChange?: (html: string, json: JSONContent) => void;
  editable?: boolean;
}

export function ResumeEditor({ content = "", onChange, editable = true }: ResumeEditorProps) {
  const editor = useEditor({
    extensions: [
      StarterKit.configure({
        heading: { levels: [1, 2, 3] },
      }),
      Placeholder.configure({
        placeholder: "Start writing...",
      }),
    ],
    content,
    editable,
    immediatelyRender: false, // REQUIRED for SSR/Next.js — prevents hydration mismatch
    editorProps: {
      attributes: {
        class: "prose prose-slate max-w-none focus:outline-none min-h-[200px] p-4",
      },
    },
    onUpdate: ({ editor }) => {
      onChange?.(editor.getHTML(), editor.getJSON());
    },
  });

  if (!editor) return null;

  return (
    <div className="border rounded-lg bg-white shadow-sm">
      {editable && <Toolbar editor={editor} />}
      <EditorContent editor={editor} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Composable API (Complex UIs with Many Child Components)

```tsx
import { Tiptap, useEditor } from "@tiptap/react";
import { BubbleMenu, FloatingMenu } from "@tiptap/react/menus";

function ComplexEditor() {
  const editor = useEditor({
    extensions: [StarterKit],
    content: "<p>Hello</p>",
    immediatelyRender: false,
  });

  if (!editor) return null;

  return (
    <Tiptap editor={editor}>
      <Tiptap.Content />
      <BubbleMenu editor={editor}>
        <FormatToolbar />
      </BubbleMenu>
      <FloatingMenu editor={editor}>
        <InsertMenu />
      </FloatingMenu>
    </Tiptap>
  );
}
```

### When to Use Each
| Feature | Composable API | Hook-Based |
|---------|---------------|------------|
| Setup complexity | Low — declarative | Medium — manual prop passing |
| Context management | Automatic | Manual via EditorContext.Provider |
| Child component access | Easy via `useTiptap()` | Requires prop drilling or context |
| Best for | Complex UIs with toolbars, sidebars, menus | Simple UIs or direct control |

## SSR / Next.js Rules

- **Always set `immediatelyRender: false`** — prevents the editor from rendering on the server
- **Always add `if (!editor) return null`** guard before rendering
- **Never import Tiptap in server components** — use `"use client"` directive
- **For server-side HTML generation**, use `generateHTML` from `@tiptap/html` (NOT from `@tiptap/core`)

## Extension Configuration

```tsx
import StarterKit from "@tiptap/starter-kit";
import Link from "@tiptap/extension-link";
import Image from "@tiptap/extension-image";
import Table from "@tiptap/extension-table";
import TableRow from "@tiptap/extension-table-row";
import TableCell from "@tiptap/extension-table-cell";
import TableHeader from "@tiptap/extension-table-header";
import { Gapcursor } from "@tiptap/extensions";

const extensions = [
  StarterKit.configure({
    heading: { levels: [1, 2, 3] },
    // Disable built-in extensions you'll replace with custom ones:
    // codeBlock: false,
  }),
  Link.configure({
    openOnClick: false,
    autolink: true,
    HTMLAttributes: { class: "text-blue-600 underline cursor-pointer" },
  }),
  Image.configure({
    inline: false,
    allowBase64: false,
  }),
  Table.configure({ resizable: true }),
  TableRow,
  TableHeader,
  TableCell,
  Gapcursor, // prevents cursor from getting stuck after tables
];
```

## Custom Extensions

```tsx
import { Node, mergeAttributes } from "@tiptap/core";
import { ReactNodeViewRenderer } from "@tiptap/react";
import { NodeViewWrapper, NodeViewContent } from "@tiptap/react";

const ResumeSection = Node.create({
  name: "resumeSection", // used as type key in JSON — NEVER rename in production without migration
  group: "block",
  content: "block+",

  addAttributes() {
    return {
      sectionType: {
        default: "experience",
        parseHTML: (element) => element.getAttribute("data-section-type"),
        renderHTML: (attributes) => ({ "data-section-type": attributes.sectionType }),
      },
    };
  },

  parseHTML() {
    return [{ tag: 'div[data-type="resume-section"]' }];
  },

  renderHTML({ HTMLAttributes }) {
    return ["div", mergeAttributes({ "data-type": "resume-section" }, HTMLAttributes), 0];
  },

  addNodeView() {
    return ReactNodeViewRenderer(ResumeSectionView);
  },
});

function ResumeSectionView({ node, updateAttributes }: NodeViewProps) {
  return (
    <NodeViewWrapper className="resume-section border-l-2 border-blue-500 pl-4 my-4">
      <div className="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase mb-2">{node.attrs.sectionType}</div>
      <NodeViewContent className="content" />
    </NodeViewWrapper>
  );
}
```

### Custom Extension Rules
- **`name` is your data contract** — once documents are stored, renaming requires a content migration
- **Design the schema first** — changing attributes or content rules later means migrating stored documents
- **Sanitize user input in `renderHTML`** — never trust `href`, `src`, or `style` attributes from pasted content
- **Use `transformPastedHTML`** to sanitize clipboard data before it enters the document
- **Use `mergeAttributes`** for composing HTML attributes safely
- **Store a version number** in document metadata for future migration support

## Content Serialization

### Client-Side (Browser)

```tsx
// Get content
const json = editor.getJSON();     // JSONContent — preferred for storage
const html = editor.getHTML();     // HTML string — useful for email/export
const text = editor.getText();     // Plain text — useful for search indexing

// Set content
editor.commands.setContent(json);   // from JSON
editor.commands.setContent(html);   // from HTML
editor.commands.clearContent();     // empty the editor
```

### Server-Side (Node.js / Edge)

```tsx
// IMPORTANT: use @tiptap/html for server — @tiptap/core is browser-only
import { generateHTML, generateJSON } from "@tiptap/html";
import StarterKit from "@tiptap/starter-kit";

// Must pass the SAME extensions the editor uses
const extensions = [StarterKit, Link, Image];

const html = generateHTML(jsonContent, extensions);
const json = generateJSON(htmlString, extensions);
```

### Static Rendering (for SSR/React)

```tsx
import { renderToReactElement } from "@tiptap/static-renderer";

// Converts ProseMirror JSON directly to React elements — no dangerouslySetInnerHTML needed
const element = renderToReactElement(jsonContent, extensions);
```

### Serialization Rules
- **Always pass the same extension array** to `generateHTML`/`generateJSON` that the editor uses — missing extensions silently drop content
- **`generateHTML` from `@tiptap/core`** is browser-only; **`generateHTML` from `@tiptap/html`** works on server
- **Prefer JSON for storage** — easier to query, transform, and migrate
- **Use `@tiptap/static-renderer`** for SSR to avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`
- **NodeView wrappers are NOT included** in `generateHTML` output — style against static output, not editor view

## Toolbar Pattern

```tsx
import { type Editor } from "@tiptap/react";

interface ToolbarProps {
  editor: Editor;
}

export function Toolbar({ editor }: ToolbarProps) {
  return (
    <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-1 border-b p-2">
      <ToolbarButton
        onClick={() => editor.chain().focus().toggleBold().run()}
        isActive={editor.isActive("bold")}
        label="Bold"
      />
      <ToolbarButton
        onClick={() => editor.chain().focus().toggleItalic().run()}
        isActive={editor.isActive("italic")}
        label="Italic"
      />
      <ToolbarButton
        onClick={() => editor.chain().focus().toggleHeading({ level: 2 }).run()}
        isActive={editor.isActive("heading", { level: 2 })}
        label="H2"
      />
      <ToolbarButton
        onClick={() => editor.chain().focus().toggleBulletList().run()}
        isActive={editor.isActive("bulletList")}
        label="List"
      />
    </div>
  );
}

function ToolbarButton({ onClick, isActive, label }: {
  onClick: () => void;
  isActive: boolean;
  label: string;
}) {
  return (
    <button
      type="button"
      onClick={onClick}
      className={cn(
        "px-2 py-1 rounded text-sm",
        isActive ? "bg-blue-100 text-blue-700" : "hover:bg-gray-100"
      )}
    >
      {label}
    </button>
  );
}
```

### Toolbar Rules
- **Always call `.focus()` before commands** — clicking a toolbar button moves focus out of the editor
- **Use `.chain()...run()`** to batch multiple commands in one transaction
- **Use `editor.isActive()`** to reflect current formatting state in the toolbar UI
- **Use `editor.can().chain().focus().toggleBold().run()`** to disable buttons when a command can't apply

## Performance

### useEditorState (Hook-Based)

```tsx
import { useEditorState } from "@tiptap/react";

function FormattingIndicator({ editor }: { editor: Editor }) {
  const { isBold, isItalic } = useEditorState({
    editor,
    selector: (ctx) => ({
      isBold: ctx.editor.isActive("bold"),
      isItalic: ctx.editor.isActive("italic"),
    }),
  });
  // Only re-renders when bold/italic state actually changes
}
```

### useTiptapState (Composable API)

```tsx
import { useTiptapState } from "@tiptap/react";

function FormattingIndicator() {
  const isBold = useTiptapState((ctx) => ctx.editor.isActive("bold"));
  // Only re-renders when bold state changes
}
```

### Performance Rules
- **Use `useEditorState` / `useTiptapState`** for selective state subscriptions — prevents full re-renders on every keystroke
- **Debounce `onUpdate` callbacks** (200-300ms) when persisting to database or triggering expensive operations
- **Avoid `trackNodeViewPosition`** unless strictly necessary — it causes per-keystroke position recalculation
- **Split toolbar into smaller components** each subscribing to only their relevant state
- **Memoize extension arrays** — recreating on every render causes editor reinitialization

## Cursor and Selection

```tsx
editor.commands.focus();                    // restore focus
editor.commands.focus("start");             // cursor to start
editor.commands.focus("end");               // cursor to end
editor.commands.focus(10);                  // cursor to position 10
editor.commands.setTextSelection(10);       // set cursor position
editor.commands.setTextSelection({ from: 5, to: 10 }); // select range
```

## Integration with Resume Builder
- Store editor content as JSON in the Zustand resume store
- On content change, debounce and update the store, which triggers PDF re-render
- Map Tiptap JSON to react-pdf components for the PDF template
- Map Tiptap JSON to docx Paragraph/TextRun for DOCX export
- Keep the content transformation functions in `src/lib/export/` — separate from UI
